.TH "VIDEOTRACKLIST.REMOVETRACK_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
VideoTrackList.removetrack_event \- VideoTrackList: removetrack event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]removetrack\f[R] event is fired when a video track is removed
from a \f[CR]VideoTrackList\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqremovetrack\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onremovetrack = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]TrackEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Using \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] videoElement = document.querySelector(\(dqvideo\(dq);

videoElement.videoTracks.addEventListener(\(dqremovetrack\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaVideo track: ${event.track.label} removed\(ga);
});
.EE
.PP
Using the \f[CR]onremovetrack\f[R] event handler property (but note that
this replaces other event listeners added using
\f[CR]onremovetrack\f[R], if any):
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] videoElement = document.querySelector(\(dqvideo\(dq);

videoElement.videoTracks.onremovetrack = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaVideo track: ${event.track.label} removed\(ga);
};
.EE
